section R05Seg6
/-!
# VIII08 — the magnetic charge `sigma_b` and `R b_s(R) -> sigma_b`

`k_s(x) = x B_s(x)/((1-x) AcK(x)^2)`, so with `g_s(x) = B_s(x)/((1-x) AcK(x)^2)`,

  `R^2 K_s(R) = (1/u^2) ∫₀^u k_s`,  `u = 1/R`,

and `k_s = t g_s` with `g_s` continuous on `[0, 1/4]`.  Since `g_s(0) = B_s(0)/A0^2` and
`B_s(0) = ∫₀^a AcK(t) s(t) dt`, the second-order Taylor behaviour of the primitive gives

  `R b_s(R) = -aY(R) · R^2 K_s(R) -> -A0 · (B_s(0)/(2 A0^2)) = -[∫₀^a Ac(t) s(t) dt]/(2 A0)`.

This limit IS the definition of `sigma_b`; nothing is assumed.
-/

